From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dcasati <dcasati@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:09:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] ath12k: accept NO_IR/RADAR channels in strict chan-list
 submission

LinuxKPI now publishes NO_IR/DFS channels as passive instead of disabling
them, but ath12k_reg_prepare_channel() still rejected those flags with
-EOPNOTSUPP, which revoked TX and made wlan vap creation fail. Allow them
and pass them to firmware as passive/DFS channels like upstream ath12k.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/reg.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/reg.c b/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/reg.c
index 7177f0d9..a4b65937 100644
--- a/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/reg.c
+++ b/sys/contrib/dev/athk/ath12k/reg.c
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ ath12k_reg_prepare_channel(const struct ieee80211_channel *channel,
 {
 	u32 allowed_flags = IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_HT40 |
 		IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_80MHZ | IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_160MHZ |
-		IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_EHT;
+		IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_EHT | IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IR |
+		IEEE80211_CHAN_RADAR;
 
 	if ((channel->band != NL80211_BAND_2GHZ &&
 	     channel->band != NL80211_BAND_5GHZ) ||
@@ -135,6 +136,9 @@ ath12k_reg_prepare_channel(const struct ieee80211_channel *channel,
 	ch->allow_vht = true;
 	ch->phy_mode = channel->band == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ ?
 		MODE_11NG_HT20 : MODE_11NA_HT20;
+	ch->dfs_set = !!(channel->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_RADAR);
+	ch->is_chan_passive = !!(channel->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_IR) ||
+		ch->dfs_set;
 	return 0;
 }
 
